  "surprise": "P02/P45-family handoff, exact version of 072: halving every residual-stream write (emb, proj, fc2 weights+biases) and quartering every LayerNorm eps after the unchanged 070-claude pretraining scored 375/350/302 on seeds 0/1/2 versus 359/335/364: exact means 342.333333 versus 352.666667, -10.33 (-2.9%); paired +16/+15/-62. Discard; inside the registered -35 to +35 range (central guess +5). The eps fix worked: logged max |logit drift| was exactly 0.0 on all three seeds (072: 1.61-2.05), so the handoff was bit-exact. Yet the result nearly reproduces 072 (370/350/311; paired +11/+15/-53): pooled over both handoff runs the six seed-runs average 343 versus 070's 353, with seeds 0/1 up and seed 2 down both times. Main surprise: round-1 targets, which with a bit-exact handoff depend only on pretraining, were 289/148/138 versus 070's 200/324/206 and 072's 92/284/102. So reruns of the identical pretraining config swing round-1 targets by about +-100 per seed (GPU nondeterminism plus wall-clock step counts 4780/4706/4782 vs 4784/4750/4776), and 072's 'damaged start' was probably pretraining rerun noise, not eps drift. The registered round-1 'within noise of 070' check is uninformative at that noise level. Plasticity prediction (RL-solved above 070 on at least 2 of 3 seeds): 807/784/716 versus 788/783/838, i.e. +19/+1/-122. That is nominally 2 of 3, but seed 1 is a tie, so it is not supported as a net gain. Seed 2 grew slowly after a weak start (targets 138->239->453->716, round-2 acc 0.118 vs 0.270-0.279 on seeds 0/1), like 072's seed 2 (690 RL-solved). Pretraining matched 070: final val loss 0.0923/0.0912/0.0959 vs 0.0911/0.0913/0.0961, held-out greedy 0.9855/0.987/0.9875 vs 0.987/0.987/0.9875. Eval seed 0 ge 7/8/9/10 = 375/304/210/30 vs 359/281/201/20; seed 2 302/234/155/14. Totals 1077/1074/1030 s, no timing cost. Reading: doubling the residual writers' relative RL step size did not beat 070 on the mean in two independent 3-seed runs, so a pure handoff rescale of the writers does not reproduce the 1x/3x/10x Muon-decay gains. Checkpoint note: eps is a module attribute, not in state_dict, so offline reloads of these checkpoints must set LayerNorm eps to 2.5e-6.",
